#> must: Iowa Kansas
#> must: Montana
#> not: Kansas Montana
#> not: ERROR parsing
#> source: $!N;s/\n/ /
# 12. Join lines in pairs, like paste. Pement: sed '$!N;s/\n/ /'
# N appends the next input line to the pattern space with a newline between;
# s/\n/ / turns that newline into a space, and the pair is printed as one
# line. $!N stops N from running on the last line, where there is nothing
# to append (GNU sed would simply print it; other seds drop it).
# Try: join triples with  $!N;$!N;s/\n/ /g
$!N;s/\n/ /

#DATA
Alabama
Alaska
Iowa
Kansas
Montana
